    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3253" root="بلق" body-key="b">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلِقَ</span></b>  and 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلُقَ</span></b> : see 9. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلَقَ</span>, (S, K, &amp;c.,)
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلُقَ</span></b> , (MSb, TA,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَلْقٌ</span>, (TA,) <i>He opened</i>
a door <i>wholly:</i> (JK, S, K:) or <i>opened</i> it <i>vehemently:</i> (K:) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابلق</span></b>  signifies the same. (JK,
S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And [hence,] <i>He devirginated,</i> or <i>defloured,</i> a girl. (AA, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  Also <i>He shut,</i> or
<i>closed,</i> a door. (IF, K.) Thus it bears two contr.
significations. (K.)

